Protocol provenance:
The original jedmeng/python-oppleio project and its tinysnake/python-oppleio-legacy
fork provided the documented packet layout, command values, CRC/XOR behavior,
and device-state interpretation used as the basis for this adapter.
https://github.com/jedmeng/python-oppleio
https://github.com/tinysnake/python-oppleio-legacy

The adapter is reorganized and modified for explicit device identity, checked
lengths and CRC, read-only defaults, bounded discovery, simulation, reply
verification, and experimental SKU-specific channel research. No unmodified
upstream Python package is bundled. The Apache-2.0 license and attribution chain
are retained conservatively; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the legacy fork's
license-file and package-metadata discrepancies.

Home Assistant's Opple integration and jedmeng/homebridge-opple are referenced
for interoperability context. Other linked projects are research references,
not bundled dependencies. No GPL reference code, unlicensed project code,
proprietary vendor app code, extracted vendor profiles, APK, SDK, firmware,
logo, or original packet capture is included.

OPPLE, Huawei, HiLink, Broadlink, Home Assistant, and other product/project
names belong to their respective owners. Their use here identifies compatible
research targets and references and does not imply endorsement.

